      "Question": "The representative peak of the silicon reference material differs from the expected position by more than the tolerance. Check the wavenumber accuracy and take the necessary action.",
      "Ans": "### Final Report: Wavenumber Accuracy Verification of Silicon Reference\n\n**1. Experiment Objective**\nThe objective was to verify the wavenumber accuracy of the Raman spectrometer by measuring a silicon (Si) reference material and determining if the measured peak position aligns with the theoretical value ($520\\text{ cm}^{-1}$). If a significant discrepancy was found, the necessary action (quantifying the error for correction) was to be taken.\n\n**2. Measurement Conditions**\n- **Sample:** Silicon Reference Material.\n- **Position:** Stage coordinates $(X: 37.982, Y: 25.362)$.\n- **Z-axis:** Optimized using `run_autofocus` (final $Z = -0.0502\\text{ mm}$).\n- **Laser Power:** $15\\%$ (per recommended protocol for Si).\n- **Exposure Time:** $0.5\\text{ s}$.\n- **Acquisition Mode:** Single shot.\n\n**3. Summary of Measurement Results**\nA single high-quality spectrum was acquired from the silicon sample. The signal showed a strong, clear peak with no saturation and sufficient SNR.\n\n**4. Physical Analysis of the Spectrum**\n- **Measured Peak Position:** $511.455\\text{ cm}^{-1}$.\n- **Expected Peak Position:** $520.000\\text{ cm}^{-1}$.\n- **Wavenumber Deviation ($\\Delta\\nu$):** $-8.545\\text{ cm}^{-1}$ (The peak is shifted to the left/lower wavenumber).\n- **Peak Quality:** The peak shape is sharp and well-defined, indicating that the shift is a systematic calibration error rather than a result of poor focus or sample degradation.\n\n**5. Interpretation and Conclusion**\nThe measured silicon peak deviates from the expected value by $\\approx 8.5\\text{ cm}^{-1}$, which significantly exceeds the typical tolerance for a calibrated Raman system (usually $< \\pm 1\\text{ cm}^{-1}$). This confirms that the current spectrometer calibration is inaccurate.\n\n**6. Action Taken & Recommendations**\nSince there is no hardware-level tool available to update the internal calibration coefficients of the spectrometer in the provided interface, the \"necessary action\" taken here is the precise quantification of the systematic offset:\n- **Identified Offset:** $-8.545\\text{ cm}^{-1}$.\n- **Correction Requirement:** To obtain accurate physical results for any subsequent measurements in this session, a linear shift of $+8.545\\text{ cm}^{-1}$ must be added to all detected peak positions.\n\n**Recommendation:** The instrument requires a full recalibration using the internal software utilities or by a technician to align the CCD pixels with the Raman shift axis accurately. Until then, all data should be corrected manually using the calculated offset.",
